# Mutant 31 — R-LIST-1
# Description: the list tie-break is `id ASC` instead of `id DESC`, so links sharing the same
#   `created_at` are returned oldest-first among themselves. Links created at distinct instants (the
#   normal case over HTTP, with microsecond timestamps) are still in the right order.
# Why realistic: a tie-break added after the fact defaults to ascending; it looks harmless because
#   timestamps almost never collide in manual testing.
# Trigger (gray-box): insert two links with the same explicit `created_at`; GET /api/links -> the lower
#   id comes first, SPEC wants the higher id first.

